Z||000000||My7Fieros||04-27-2001||02:50 PM||||Ive been thinking for a while about this now...my friend has a 2001 Corvette convertible. If you're familiar w/ Vettes, on the convertible models there is whats called a "waterfall" between the seats (sorry dont have a pic, I'll go over there tomorrow and take one of it). Basically its a fiberglass piece that comes from the trunk down inside the car between the seats. Its painted the same color as the car. I thought this would look pretty cool in a Fiero (even though its not a convt). I know some of you are into the fiberglass making thing (Bam Bam just posted something about this), and wondered if any one has ever considered doing this. It would, of course, replace the plastic glove box piece between the seats. Possibly make it out of fiberglass, rounded (kinda like on the Vette), and painted to match the color of the car. Possible?  Just a thought......M7F<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||04-27-2001||03:11 PM||||I thought the same thing the first time I saw the Corvette convertable. I don't have the skills to do it, but I think that it's possible. I would suggest making it (or another part) so that it covered the top of the rear firewall along with the console. (just the part of the firewall that has the felt piece on it now)||||reg||1
